TEXT 312 288 Left 2 !vb b 0 pwl 0s 10A
TEXT 32 360 Left 2 ;Switcher mode 1:(toff high,ioff high)   toff=100m ioff=1e6 \n                           The switcher acts very smooth -> no spikes at all\nSwitcher mode 2:(toff low,ioff small)  toff=1u ioff=10A \n                            The switcher is off at i < ioff -> smaller spikes but spikes (3MV spike)\nSwitcher mode 3:(toff low,ioff high) toff=1u ioff=1e6 \n                             The switcher is off immediately (800MV spike)\n \nAt Switcher mode 2: There can be a breakpoint device helping to switch at very low currents (eg. ioff=100mA)\n                                 (very small timesteps to met the current condition at around switching time)
TEXT 160 128 Left 3 ;The best ( fastest simulation, \nno spikes ) is with Switcher mode 1 !!
